  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mekong Region: Responding to Cross Border Mobility Challenges at Points of Entry Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute to resuming cross-border mobility across GMS countries (Cambodia, Lao People&apos;s Democratic Republic, Thailand, and Viet Nam) to aid socio-economic recovery efforts from the impact of COVID-19. To achieve the intended objective, the project focuses on supporting the Governments of the GMS countries and relevant authorities at points of entry (PoEs) to effectively implement preventive and responsive measures to mitigate cross-border transmission risks of COVID-19. This will be delivered through three main interventions. Firstly, national guidelines and SOPs will be developed for PoEs stakeholders and officials of the Greater Mekong Countries to effectively manage local and international cross-border flows at land borders using a health-compliant approach to border management. Secondly, PoE stakeholders and officials of the GSM Countries will have access to necessary PPE to effectively mitigate direct and/or indirect transmission while performing their respective duties and protecting the health of travelers at land borders. Thirdly, border management officers will be provided with technical support for public health aspects of resuming border operations to improve information capture and data sharing.</narrative>
  </description>
